"""Phase A: every accepted Release Bundle in stores/, wired by dependency only.

    pixi run release OGS-00042             one release, plus any parent it needs
    pixi run release OGS-00042 OGS-00051   several; lineage order is resolved
    pixi run index                         regenerate the master list

One Snakefile for the whole registry rather than one per release, so
Snakemake's own wildcard expansion is the multi-release runner and a
Reference-Completed release can declare its parent's `register` record as a
real input edge. A batch loop would have to sequence parents before children
by hand.

Per ADR 0023 this file contains no Store Family name, no source column name,
no manifest translation, and no layout branch. Each rule asks `ogstores.plan`
for a Step and hands it to `ogstores.run`; each rule's tracked output is that
step's record file, never the Store directory -- a half-written Store must not
satisfy a rule.

    build ──> top_hits ──> rho ──> overview ──> validate ──> register

`top_hits` and `rho` are conditional on `build.yaml`'s `post` block. A
Reference-Completed release substitutes `complete` for `build` and takes the
same tail.

IMPLEMENTATION PENDING -- see docs/spec/store-release-workflow.md. The
sequencing is deliberately bundle.py + plan.py + golden argv tests first, with
no Snakefile at all, so that the seam is proven to be just an argv before any
orchestration is built on it.
"""
